# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF to disk
# while the blobs stay LF. Two gates read the working tree directly and break
# under that split:
#
#   · tests/unit/userscript-integrity.test.js hashes each published userscript
#     from disk, so its pinned SHA-256 values are only reproducible on the
#     platform that generated them.
#   · Prettier is configured with endOfLine "lf", so format:check fails on every
#     file git has rewritten.
#
# Forcing eol=lf keeps both reproducible on Windows, macOS, Linux and CI alike.
* text=auto eol=lf
